{"parentUuid":"a3e43d20-f9db-44fa-86c9-04928f9c8110","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ad6a96a2be529de3c","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfqBbmgzw4AiVduNcv2GT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AAi6XtiDk49Cj3GHaAu5ZZ","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Root cause: cuore/web/labels_routes.py builds its own Jinja2Templates instance; static_url/icon/t/lang globals were only ever registered on it as a side effect of importing cuore.web.static_version/icons/i18n, which only happens via cuore.app. check_labels.py builds a standalone minimal FastAPI app around labels_routes without importing cuore.app, so static_url (needed by base.html, and t() needed by included _vbar.html) was undefined -> 500.\n\nFix (smallest-diff): in cuore/web/labels_routes.py, right after `templates = Jinja2Templates(...)`, added side-effect imports of `.static_version`, `.icons`, `.i18n` (mirrors the existing pattern those modules already use, and is safe under Python's circular-import handling since `templates` is already bound by the time each module's by-name registration loop looks it up).\n\nAlso fixed cuore/tests/check_live_dashboard_page.py: its gauges-page assertions checked for the literal `src=\"/static/live/widgets.js\"` / `dashboard.js\"`, which now 404-proofs via static_url()'s `?v=<hash>` cache-buster, breaking the exact match. Changed both needles to prefix-match (drop the trailing `\"`) with a comment explaining why. (hud page's needles were untouched — hud is hand-built HTML, not templated, so no versioning applies there.)\n\ncheck_tools_page.py was already passing (no code issue found there; likely fixed by another agent already).\n\nVerified: check_labels.py 200/200, check_live_dashboard_page.py 19/19, check_tools_page.py 6/6, check_api.py 96/96 all green. `import cuore.app` still succeeds (no circular-import breakage).\n\nFiles touched: C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\labels_routes.py, C:\\Users\\